  "boundaries": [
    "One actual unchanged-producer control reproduces missing removal after committed canonical retirement. Compatible candidate consumer/reader context is archived; this is not an entirely unchanged-workspace run.",
    "Five actual original browser controls fail and the snapshot control passes; all six final browser controls pass. The original retained-helper witness is a naive tombstone-append design control, not a claim that baseline emitted removals.",
    "Retained streams receive valid ERC20 removal identities independently of current filters/history membership; clients ignore unknown identities. Snapshots retain only surviving previously admitted alerts and do not refill older evictions.",
    "Exact newly retired row IDs are selected in the existing scan. Segment identity and ownership protect post-commit row/page-batched materialization; existing raw column buffers and selected metadata remain per-segment costs, without a fixed-byte or global RSS bound.",
    "The initial worker rewrite was rejected by automatic approval review; the user subsequently explicitly approved the concrete local change and offline cancellation tests. Preserve both records and final independent lifecycle review.",
    "Publication follows successful complete retirement. A later materialization failure can follow earlier committed removal batches and is terminal to the engine; no atomic network frame, exactly-once delivery or restart replay is promised.",
    "Historical backfill remains silent; ordinary forward notification follows accepted visible ingestion with existing bounded recovery semantics, not a new per-batch fsync barrier.",
    "No persisted format, dependency, SQL implementation, production dataset, live sync, remote-host work or benchmark change. Shared budgets, dashboard review, verified offline repair and integrated acceptance remain open."
  ]
